{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00741 - MONDO_5480",
  "verbalization": "Hydrocortisone is implicated in the development of Contact Dermatitis through a series of indirect pathways involving inflammatory conditions. The evidence suggests that Hydrocortisone is associated with Chronic Cutaneous Lupus Erythematosus, a condition that is itself linked to Prednicarbate and Desoximetasone, both of which are indicated to cause Contact Dermatitis. This implies that Hydrocortisone may exert a therapeutic or contributory effect on the inflammatory processes underlying Contact Dermatitis, possibly through its anti-inflammatory properties. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Hydrocortisone to Contact Dermatitis highlights a potential role in the pathogenesis of the condition, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The overlapping indications suggest a broader pharmacological profile that may contribute to the development of contact dermatitis in various contexts.",
